From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6375: add the TCSR download mode address

Without it, qcom_scm has no way to touch download mode at all:

	qcom_scm firmware:scm: No available mechanism for setting download mode

qcom_scm_set_download_mode() wants either an SCM call this firmware does not
offer, or a register named by qcom,dload-mode, and sm6375.dtsi provides neither.
That message is printed only when download mode was asked for; the rest of the
time the driver silently cannot clear it either, which is the more interesting
half.

The register is the same one the rest of this family uses. agatti.dtsi, which
is qcm2290, carries

	qcom,dload-mode = <&tcsr_regs 0x13000>;

added in commit dc231840dca6 ("arm64: dts: qcom: qcm2290: Add TCSR download
mode address"), whose reasoning applies here word for word: it is "especially
useful for a clean watchdog reset without entry into download mode", and the
gap went unnoticed because the error was suppressed.

sm6375 had no TCSR syscon at all to point at, so add one. The base is confirmed
twice over: sm6115.dtsi has tcsr_regs at 0x3c0000 with a size of 0x40000, and
agatti.dtsi has it at the same address, while all three SoCs place tcsr_mutex
at 0x340000. 0x13000 is well inside 0x40000, and nothing else in sm6375.dtsi
claims anything between 0x340000 and 0x4411000.

Tested on a Motorola Moto G82 5G (SM6375), where the point of it is a silent
reset that leaves nothing behind: bootreason=watchdog, an empty pstore every
time, and the reserved ramoops and debug carveouts holding uninitialised DRAM
rather than data. The PMIC records those resets as PS_HOLD, meaning the SoC
asked to go down rather than the PMIC deciding, so the reset path runs through
the secure world, and being unable to tell it which kind of reset to perform is
a plausible reason for DDR not surviving.
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375.dtsi
@@ -307,6 +307,7 @@
 			compatible = "qcom,scm-sm6375", "qcom,scm";
 			clocks = <&rpmcc RPM_SMD_CE1_CLK>;
 			clock-names = "core";
+			qcom,dload-mode = <&tcsr_regs 0x13000>;
 			#reset-cells = <1>;
 		};
 	};
@@ -823,6 +824,11 @@
 			#hwlock-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
+		tcsr_regs: syscon@3c0000 {
+			compatible = "qcom,sm6375-tcsr", "syscon";
+			reg = <0x0 0x003c0000 0x0 0x40000>;
+		};
+
 		tlmm: pinctrl@500000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,sm6375-tlmm";
 			reg = <0 0x00500000 0 0x800000>;
